	{{block('/-/block/hero_full.html?variant=7-9aefeec9dd-nfjh13')}}
	<div style="background-color:;display:block !important;" class="p-6 rounded-5 bg-light mb-18" data-zesty-id="design:columns:1 Column:67:80">
<div style="flex:1" className={styles.pvlColumn} class="column" data-zesty-id="design:columns:1 Column:67:80-1:1 Column:0">
<img src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/uss-cache.salvationarmy.org/f7191a06-52f1-42df-bbbc-363c47140dba_New+Building+Photos.jpg" alt="placeholder" class="img-fluid d-block my-3" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;" loading="lazy" / data-zesty-id="content:images:2:51">
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:4:68"></div>
<h5 data-zesty-id="content:text:5:67">What We Do</h5>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:6:54">
	We offer a place for those experiencing&nbsp;homelessness and poverty to get help.
</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:7:61">
	We provide low barrier access, free of charge, to the following basic daily amenities:<span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;"></span>
</p>
<ul data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:8:95">
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Hot breakfast </span><span style="color:#ed1c2b;"><span lang="ES">(Monday, Wednesday, and Friday starting at 9:00 a.m.)</span></span><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;"></span></li>
	<li>Food pantry</li>
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Case management</span></li>
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Clothing vouchers through The Salvation Army Thrift Store</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:9:32"></div>
<h5 data-zesty-id="content:text:11:65"><span style="color:#ed1c2b;">New Location</span></h5>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:12:49"><span style="color:#ed1c2b;">1740 S. Horner Blvd.</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:13:14">Sanford, NC 27330</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:14:78"><a href="tel:9197181717">(919) 718-1717</a></span></p>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:15:49"></div>
<p data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:16:60">
	To learn more, follow us on Facebook <a href="https://www.facebook.com/NavCenterLeeCo" target="">@TheSalvationArmyLeeCountyNC</a>
</p>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:17:7"></div>
<h5 data-zesty-id="content:text:19:20">Hours</h5>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:20:18">
	Monday - Thursday&nbsp;9 a.m. - 12:00&nbsp;p.m. and 1:00 p.m. - 4:00 p.m.&nbsp;
</p>
<div class="my-4" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-md:21:57"></div>
<h5 data-zesty-id="content:text:22:83">Who We Are</h5>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:23:39">
	The Salvation Army of Lee County Service Center connects&nbsp;individuals living in homelessness, or on the edge of homelessness, with resources that will guide them in re-establishing and maintaining equilibrium in their lives. We refer clients to a variety of partners depending on client need.&nbsp;Our array of supporters help individuals navigate from crisis to stability by providing:
</p>
<ul data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:24:44">
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Medical services</span></li>
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Mental health support and services</span></li>
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Peer support for those in active addiction</span></li>
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Shelter and housing</span></li>
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Job searches and resume writing</span></li>
	<li><span lang="ES" style="color:#202124;">Veterans services</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:25:86"></div>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:26:96">
	Our services are&nbsp;focused on bridging the gap that exists between the needs of&nbsp;clients and&nbsp;available resources in Lee County.
</p>
<div class="my-4" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-md:27:64"></div>
<img src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/uss-cache.salvationarmy.org/7026ed5e-845c-4521-96a3-786b723cff9e_Vicky+Dorothy+Amanda+food+pantry+04222025.jpg" alt="placeholder" class="img-fluid d-block my-3" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;" loading="lazy" / data-zesty-id="content:images:27:24">
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:29:87"></div>
<h5 data-zesty-id="content:text:30:19">Donate</h5>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:31:17">
	Our work is only possible through the generous support of donors like you.
</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:32:6">
	We rely on contributions of non-perishable food, breakfast foods, ground coffee, cleaning supplies, disposable plates and tableware, and personal hygiene items.
</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:33:98">
	Financial support is always welcomed and needed.
</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:34:12">
	To donate, you may do so <a href="https://give.salvationarmyusa.org/give/164006/#!/donation/checkout" target="">online</a> or please call <a href="tel:9197181717">919-718-1717</a>.<br>
	&nbsp;
</p>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:35:99"></div>
<h5 data-zesty-id="content:text:36:73">Volunteer</h5>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:37:43">
	We could not operate without the compassionate efforts of our dedicated volunteers.
</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:textarea:38:2">
	Our volunteers help prepare breakfast weekdays from 8:15&nbsp;a.m. - 10:00 a.m., and assist clients as needed.
</p>
<p data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:39:54">
	To join them, please contact our Volunteer Coordinator Beth Bray, <a href="mailto:Beth.Bray@uss.salvationarmy.org" target="">beth.bray@uss.salvationarmy.org</a>.
</p>
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:40:82"></div>
